        "decision": "No SQLite. drills/*.json stays the source of truth and no database is wired in. The file layout IS the product's agent route: Claude/Codex author drill files directly on a subscription (no API costs), chokidar pushes SSE so files appear in the library in about a second, git gives history/diff/backup, and a coach can eyeball or hand-edit any drill. A binary store would subtract every one of those properties and add a native dependency (better-sqlite3 compiles against the Node ABI) to gain indexes and transactions that a personal library measured in tens of files cannot feel. In-memory search over library summaries is already instant at this scale.",
